Rejoignez SafranTech, le pôle de recherche du groupe Safran, et contribuez à explorer, évaluer et transformer les technologies d'IA les plus avancées en démonstrateurs à fort potentiel pour l'ensemble du groupe.
Nous recherchons un(e)Research Scientist / Engineer doté(e) d'une solide expertise scientifique, capable de faire le pont entre la recherche de pointe et l'expérimentation concrète. Votre mission ne sera pas de produire des solutions industrielles finalisées, mais de transformer des technologies de rupture — en particulier autour des LLM et des systèmes agentiques — en POC et démonstrateurs qui éclairent les choix technologiques du groupe.
Il s'agit d'un poste exploratoire et transverse, à la frontière entre la recherche académique et l'ingénierie, avec une réelle autonomie sur vos axes d'investigation.
Vos missions : 
- Explorer et évaluer les technologies émergentes en IA générative, LLM, agents et agent harness ;
- Concevoir et développer des POC et démonstrateurs permettant de valider la faisabilité et la valeur de ces technologies pour les métiers du groupe ;
- Réaliser une veille scientifique et technologique active sur vos domaines d'expertise, et en restituer les enseignements auprès des équipes ;
- Représenter SafranTech lors de conférences scientifiques et techniques, et entretenir un réseau au sein des écosystèmes de recherche et industriels ;
- Être force de proposition sur les orientations technologiques et les opportunités d'application des IA génératives au sein du groupe ;
- Documenter et diffuser vos travaux (rapports, publications éventuelles, retours d'expérience) auprès des équipes de recherche et des métiers.
 Nous recherchons avant tout les qualités et compétences suivantes :
- Vous disposez d'une expertise scientifique solide, avec le goût de l'expérimentation et de la démonstration de concepts ;
- Vous êtes passionné·e par l'IA et suivez de près ses évolutions ;
- Vous maîtrisez les outils LLM et connaissez en profondeur l'écosystème agentique actuel (agents, orchestration, harness) ;
- Vous êtes à l'aise avec les outils de développement assisté par IA (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode...) et les exploitez au quotidien ;
- Vous savez transformer une idée ou un article de recherche en prototype fonctionnel rapidement ;
- Vous êtes autonome, curieux·se et force de proposition ;
- Vous avez de bonnes qualités de communication, à l'écrit comme à l'oral, pour présenter vos travaux en interne comme en conférence.

Location 
ESTEC, Noordwijk, Netherlands 
 Description 
 Galileo Services Implementation Lead in the Galileo System Engineering Unit, Galileo System Engineering Service, Galileo Programme Office, Galileo and EGNOS Programme Department, Directorate of Resilience, Navigation and Connectivity.
Galileo is Europe’s own global navigation satellite system providing a highly accurate, guaranteed global positioning service under civilian control. It is already the world’s most precise satellite navigation system with a base of more than 4 billion users.
The Galileo System Engineering Unit oversees the definition and specification of the Galileo system releases, known as system builds, which respond to growing mission needs in terms of positioning accuracy, availability, integrity, assurance, robustness, and emergency response. This encompasses the definition of the new Galileo Second Generation satellites (with the first batch under development), the updates of the current Galileo First Generation fleet, the necessary updates to the ground segment, coordination with service facilities and with external entities, and the management of the planning and delivery of the system builds to the EU as the owner and service provider.
You will be responsible for the capture and implementation of stakeholders’ service provision requirements in the Galileo system, the Galileo project’s contribution to the service roadmaps, service KPIs and their measurement. You will establish and coordinate activities within the programme and with industrial consortiums and liaise with entities within and outside the Agency in the performance of your duties.
You will interact with a very talented group of engineers in the Systems Engineering Unit and in the Galileo project as a whole.
 Duties 
 Your tasks and responsibilities will include the following:
 leading the definition of the Galileo system roadmap, defining capabilities for each system build, contributing to the alignment between the Galileo system roadmap and the programme and service roadmaps for Galileo, and maintaining the statement of compliance with the service provision requirements throughout the Galileo lifecycle;
 representing ESA as design and/or qualification authority vis-à-vis the European Union and its agencies (Commission/EUSPA) and Member States for the capture and implementation of GNSS service provision requirements, in direct coordination with all stakeholders, delegated from the Galileo Programme Office;
 leading the identification and description of new user segment use cases, validating the completion of the Galileo System specification from a service provision point of view, and proposing updates when relevant;
 managing the weekly interactions with Commission/EUSPA/Member States with respect to the design of the different system builds and the associated commitment in terms of statements of compliance with Galileo services;
 contributing to the definition of the Galileo system requirements, the system architecture and operations concept in line with the service provision requirements and the Galileo system roadmap;
 contributing to the System Assembly, Integration and Verification Plan and its implementation in the area of user performance/service verification and validation;
 contributing to the investigation and closure of ARs and NCRs related to your area of expertise throughout the entire Galileo lifecycle;
 contributing to, and leading when required, the definition and implementation of studies, tools and testbeds to demonstrate, prototype and validate user performance for identified and new use cases;
 coordinating with the Space Segment, Ground Segment and the System Security teams, the System Assembly, Integration and Verification and the PA and Safety teams, the Project Office, the Management Support Office and industry to ensure the proper implementation of the Galileo system roadmap;
 ensuring that ESA's role as Galileo design authority and system development prime contractor is maintained throughout;
 representing ESA vis-à-vis the European Union, EU Member States, international authorities and bodies, for example in mission consolidation reviews, service reviews and working groups;
 ensuring technical synergy and coordination with other EU and ESA PNT programmes;
 identifying lessons learned and contributing to the knowledge management initiatives in the Directorate.
 Technical competencies 
 Knowledge of GNSS systems and services, user equivalent range error and sensor fusion
 Knowledge and experience of GNSS receivers and GNSS user segment applications such as high-accuracy mass-market applications, autonomous vehicles and/or timing and synchronisation
 Experience in design, development and validation for large space projects
 Experience in product roadmapping
 Experience in coordinating the work of technical experts
 Experience in management of industry contracts for technology and product development
 Behavioural competencies 
 Result …

Location 
ESTEC, Noordwijk, Netherlands 
 Description 
 Launch Services and Technical Coordinator in the Earth Observation Projects Department, Directorate of Earth Observation Programmes.
Reporting to the Earth Explorer Missions Programme Manager, you, as Launch Services Coordinator, will be in charge of the tasks related to the coordination of the procurement and assessment of launch services for the Earth Explorers, SCOUTs, some Earth Watch missions and VIGIL as well as for selected projects of the European Resilience from Space for Earth Observation programme. Furthermore, you will act as back-up for the launch services coordinator for the Copernicus missions. For the missions to which the postholder will be assigned in time sharing, you will be responsible as Technical Officer for the launch service contracts, supporting the execution of the launch services related activities from the initial feasibility studies to (and including) launch campaigns. You will follow the technical definition of the I/F between the spacecraft and their related launch vehicles and, working across more projects, you will aim to optimize and harmonize technical solutions and contractual arrangements between projects and launcher providers. You will also advise each mission on the launcher related activities of the spacecraft industrial contractors. For the execution of these tasks, you will report functionally to the respective project managers and work in close collaboration with the project teams.
You will provide support to the Head of the Earth Observation Projects Department in establishing and maintaining technical and programmatic dossiers related to launchers and launch services. You will also act as the contact point with the Collective Launcher Service Procurement and other Directorate of Space Transportation representatives.
As Technical Coordinator, you will support the definition and coherent implementation of applicable policies and common technical solutions across the projects. Your responsibilities will also include acting as technical representative for the Earth Observation Projects Department as regards the definition and adoption of some common developments, new technologies and methodologies, and the follow-up of the implementation by the missions.
 Duties 
 Your principal tasks and responsibilities will include:
 acting as the focal point at Earth Explorer Missions Programme level for all launcher activities in the relations with the launcher authorities;
 establishing and maintaining technical and programmatic dossiers related to launchers and launch services relevant for the Earth Explorer, SCOUT, some Earth Watch and other relevant missions, including selected missions of the European Resilience from Space for Earth Observation programme and (as back-up) for some Copernicus missions;
 monitoring the evolution of the worldwide commercial and institutional launch service market and launch vehicle performances relevant for the Earth Explorer, SCOUT, some Earth Watch and other relevant missions;
 supporting the Earth Explorer, SCOUT, Earth Watch and other relevant missions in the establishment and monitoring of launch services, by acting as Technical Officer of related contracts ensuring coordination with other relevant Directorates:
 supporting the procurement of the launcher vehicle and services, supporting in the negotiation of the relevant launch services contracts;
 providing technical support and expertise for launcher I/F definition and launch services procurement;
 providing support for the technical activities to be conducted with the launcher providers such as mission feasibility studies, engineering analyses, PMARs and FMARs;
 providing support for the interface definition between the launch service provider authorities and the satellite prime contractor in order to ensure technical and programmatic viability, completeness of documentations and the adequacy of the I/F verification;
 participating as Earth Explorer Missions Programme representative in various launch vehicles reviews (e.g. LV qualification review, failure reviews, etc.);
 providing support in the preparation of the launch campaign, monitoring also the industrial activities including planning, transport, logistic and definition of launch site activities;
 acting as ESA Deputy Launch Campaign Manager during the Earth Explorer missions launch campaigns.
 establishing, consolidating and maintaining a list of common technical topics and methodologies that would be candidates for a coordinated implementation approach within the Earth Explorer, SCOUT, some EarthWatch and other relevant missions;
 coordinating the assessment of the identified common technical topics involving the relevant projects teams, as well as relevant experts from other ESA mission project teams, departments or directorates, as applicable;
 supporting the relevant projects teams in the implementation of common technical topics;
 supporting the relevant project …

