Concevoir et développer des applications GenAI intégrant des LLM, en exploitant leurs capacités de raisonnement, de génération et d’utilisation d’outils. Développer des agents IA et des workflows agentiques avec LangChain et LangGraph : orchestration, gestion d’état, mémoire, tool calling, exécution de tâches complexes et gestion des erreurs. Concevoir des architectures d’intégration via MCP (Model Context Protocol) afin de connecter les agents IA aux API, bases de données, outils et services métiers. Développer des API et des services backend en Python avec FastAPI pour exposer les fonctionnalités IA, gérer les interactions avec les modèles et faciliter leur intégration dans les systèmes existants. Construire et industrialiser des pipelines IA : gestion des prompts, intégration des modèles, traitement des données, orchestration des appels LLM et mise en place de mécanismes de fallback. Déployer et maintenir les solutions en production en intégrant les composants IA dans des architectures robustes, scalables et observables, avec une attention particulière portée à la performance et à la disponibilité. Évaluer et optimiser les systèmes GenAI à travers la conception de jeux de tests, le suivi de la qualité des réponses, la mesure des performances et la maîtrise des coûts d’inférence. Garantir la sécurité et la fiabilité des applications IA : gestion des accès, protection des données, validation des entrées et sorties, traçabilité des interactions et maîtrise des risques liés aux agents autonomes. Contribuer à l’évolution de la plateforme IA en expérimentant de nouveaux modèles, frameworks et patterns d’architecture, puis en industrialisant les solutions les plus pertinentes.

About Us 
 The European Molecular Biology Laboratory (EMBL) is one of the world's leading basic research institutions in the life sciences. In addition to its main laboratory in Heidelberg, EMBL operates sites in Hinxton (EMBL-EBI, United Kingdom), Grenoble (France), Hamburg (Germany), Barcelona (Spain) and Rome (Italy).
 Your Role 
 The Facility Management team at EMBL's Heidelberg headquarters is at the start of implementing a CAFM system – and you'll play a leading role in shaping that process. Reporting to the Head of Facility Management, you will:
 Actively help design, structure and roll out the new CAFM system, including the data model and process definitions;
 Capture, prepare and maintain building and technical services plans in the BIM model, and migrate existing 2D records into Revit;
 Integrate building services planning (HVAC/electrical) into existing architectural models and floor plans;
 Produce execution plans for refurbishments and renovations across construction and lab-building projects;
 Collaborate with in-house architects as well as external planning offices and specialist engineers.
 You have 
 Completed training as a building technician, technical systems planner (building services, equipment or electrical engineering), or draughtsperson;
 At least 5 years of professional experience, ideally at a planning office in architecture, building services or electrical engineering;
 Confident use of Autodesk Revit (2D/3D); working in BIM is a firm requirement for this role;
 Experience with AutoCAD and solid handling of DWG/DXF files;
 Experience with the implementation or rollout of a CAFM system is a clear plus;
 Basic knowledge of structural engineering and building physics, with cross-trade understanding;
 Confident handling of DIN standards and construction scheduling;
 Good spatial visualization skills;
 Good written and spoken German and/or English;
 Willingness for ongoing professional development, particularly in BIM/CAFM.
 What We Offer 
 From day one, you'll take on real responsibility – not support work, but your own projects. Flexible hours, short decision paths, and a team that backs each other up rather than just clocking in and out. We're on the verge of implementing a CAFM system – you won't just be a user, you'll help shape how processes, data structures and standards look going forward. Your experience and input feed directly into decisions that will shape Facility Management for years to come. Further training here isn't just talk – it's part of the job.
 EMBL is committed to equal opportunity – what matters to us is what you can do.
 Contract duration: 3 years (renewable up to 9 in total)
 Salary: Grade 4, monthly salary from 3.812,27 after tax, plus generous benefits and financial allowances based on individual circumstances. Excluding 12.99% personal pension and insurance contributions. 
 Why join us 
EMBL is curiosity-driven, community-oriented and international. As an inclusive, equal opportunity employer, we believe that diversity enables us to collaborate more effectively and be innovative in our approaches. We are, therefore, committed to creating an inclusive and flexible culture - one where everyone can realise their full potential and make a positive contribution to our organisation. 
 We encourage applications from individuals who can complement our existing team – we believe that success is built on having teams whose backgrounds and personal experiences reflect the diversity of the populations that our science serves. We actively encourage applications from all genders and cultures, ethnic groups and all demographics to help us avoid perpetuating biases and oversights at this transformational point in our people strategy.
 Enjoy lots of benefits: 
 Financial incentives: Salary free of income tax, Monthly family, child and non-resident allowances, annual salary review, pension scheme, death benefit, long-term care, accident-at-work and unemployment insurances
 Flexible working arrangements 
 Private medical insurance for you and your immediate family (including all prescriptions and generous dental & optical cover)
 Generous time off: 30 days annual leave per year, in addition to public holidays
 Relocation package including installation grant (conditions apply) 
 Campus life: Free shuttle bus (Heidelberg), library, subsidised on-site cafeteria, casual dress code, extensive sports and social club activities (on campus and remotely)
 Family benefits: Kindergarten (Heidelberg), 10 days of child sick leave, generous paid maternity/parental leave and monthly family & child allowances
 Benefits for international newcomers: Visa exemption, education grant for private schooling, financial support to travel back to your home country every second year and a monthly non-resident allowance.
